R"VG(
# minutes.vg (H-04, the second pass): the minutes of a meeting (a council's, a board's, a committee's: the items, who said what, what
# was decided, which was usually nothing). An item is built from parts (what was raised, about what, where; who spoke and how; what
# came of it), each people keeping its own few ways of putting each part (`people=K`), so one council "carries" a motion by a show of
# hands and another "lets it stand"; their disputes are their own: their water, their herds in the streets, their crafts' smells.
# The manual is manual.vg's.

genre.minutes (words=26..146)
  {min.head}\n{min.item}\n{min.item}\n{min.item}\n{min.close}
  {min.head}\n{min.present}\n{min.item}\n{min.item}\n{min.close}
  {min.head}\n{min.item}\n{min.item}\n{min.item}\n{min.item}\n{min.close}
  {min.head}\n{min.present}\n{min.item}\n{min.item}\n{min.item}\n{min.close}

min.head (formula people=3)
  Minutes of the meeting of the {min.body} of {$home}, held in {season.now}, year {#year:digits}.
  {min.body} of {$home}: minutes.
  The {min.body} met at {$home} in {season.now}. These are the minutes.
  Minutes, {min.body}, {$home}, {season.now}.
  Record of the {min.body} of {$home}, its meeting of {season.now}.

min.body (people=3)
  council
  water board
  school committee
  market board
  street committee
  residents' association
  {craft} guild
  (coast=1) harbour board
  (has:assembly) assembly
  (has:company) board of {company}

# ---- who was there -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

min.present
  Present: {min.who}, {min.who2} and {#n|member}. {min.absent}
  {#n|member} present, with {min.gallery}{min.present2}. {min.absent}
  Present: {min.who}, {min.who2}, and {min.extra}. {min.absent}
min.who (people=3)
  the chair
  the secretary
  the treasurer
  the clerk
  the eldest member
  the member for the north side
min.who2 (people=3)
  the keeper of the seal
  the clerk of the works
  the member for {$home}
  the doctor
  the schoolmaster
  the {craft} guild's member
  the harbour master
min.present2
  (3)
  , and the windows open
  , the stove lit for once
  , under the {craft} guild's banner
  , and {drink} on the side table
min.gallery (people=4)
  the public gallery full
  the gallery empty but for a dog
  two reporters in the gallery
  the gallery full of {craft} workers
  a crowd outside
  the children of the members in the gallery
  a smell of {food} from the gallery
  the gallery asked to keep its voice down
  half the {craft} guild in the gallery
  the gallery cold and the windows open
min.extra (people=2)
  one who was asked to leave
  a visitor from {$seat}, who said nothing
  the new member, who said a great deal
  a child who was looking for a parent
min.absent (people=3)
  Apologies from the rest.
  The member for the north side was absent again.
  One seat is empty since {season.any}.
  The clerk was late.
  Two absent through sickness.
  Absent without word: the usual.

# ---- an item ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

min.item
  (3) Item: {min.topic}. {min.outcome}
  (2) On {min.topic}, {min.speaker} {min.said}. {min.outcome}
  (2) The chair raised {min.topic}. {min.outcome}
  A letter from {min.from} about {min.tobj} was read. {min.outcome}
  {min.speaker} asked that {min.tobj} be put on the next agenda. {min.short}
  On {min.topic}, {min.speaker} {min.said}; {min.speaker2} {min.said2}. {min.outcome}
  (stage>=1) Item: the closing of the {min.building} on the hill. Agreed. Nobody spoke.
  (stage>=2) Item: the evacuation plan. The chair asked whether anyone had read it. Nobody had.

min.topic
  {min.tpre} {min.tobj} {min.tpost}
min.tpre (people=6)
  the matter of
  complaints about
  the cost of
  a petition about
  the state of
  the question of
  the future of
  a report on
  a dispute over
  an inquiry into
  the old quarrel over
  a proposal about
  the money for
  a letter of thanks for
min.tobj (share=0.7)
  the drains
  the {craft} works
  the {watersrc.n}
  the old {min.building}
  the {festival} procession
  the market stalls
  the {herd} kept in the town
  {streets.of}
  {town.edge}
  {town.open}
  the ground for {pastime}
  the bridge over {river}
  the {tree} along the river road
  the tram shelters
  the public baths
  the burial ground
  the {colour.any} doors of the old houses
  the stores of {food}
  the {drink} houses
  the fountain
  the clock
  the bells
  (coast=1) the harbour wall
  (coast=1) the fish market
  (has:$home.landmark) {$home.landmark}
min.tpost (people=5)
  (4)
  , again
  , raised before
  , for the third time this year
  (has:$home.quarter) in {$home.quarter}
  (has:$home.quarter) near {$home.quarter}
  on the north side
  by the station
  , which the members had hoped was settled
min.building (people=2)
  school
  hall
  baths
  library
  clinic
  market
  orphanage
  fire station

min.from (people=4)
  {$seat}
  a resident of {$home}
  the {craft} guild
  the schoolchildren of {$home}
  a lawyer acting for the {craft} works
  the keeper of {holyplace}
  the widows of the {craft} workers
  a traveller from {city2}
  the {herd} keepers' society

min.speaker (people=4)
  the treasurer
  the secretary
  the oldest member
  a visitor from {$seat}
  the youngest member
  the member who keeps {herd}
  the {craft} guild's member
  the doctor
  the clerk of the works
  (has:$home.quarter) the member for {$home.quarter}
min.speaker2 (people=3)
  the chair
  another member
  the treasurer
  the visitor
  the clerk
min.said (people=6)
  said that it had been raised before
  proposed that it be dropped
  asked who was paying for it
  reminded the meeting of the last time
  spoke for some time
  said that the old way had worked well enough
  said that the people of {$home} would not stand for it
  proposed a committee to look into it
  wished it minuted that the member had warned them
  said nothing, at length
  quoted the old saying: {proverb}
  said that {ruler.the} would have to be told
  read out a list of figures nobody could follow
  asked whether anyone had been to look
min.said2 (people=3)
  disagreed
  agreed, for once
  asked for the figures
  left the room
  said the same, more loudly
  called for a vote

min.outcome
  (5) {min.short}
  (2) {min.long}
min.short (people=5)
  Agreed.
  Deferred.
  Noted.
  Agreed, one against.
  Carried.
  Lost.
  Let stand.
  Not agreed.
  Withdrawn.
  Passed by hands.
  Referred back.
min.long (share=0.8)
  Agreed, after {min.delay}.
  Deferred until {min.until}.
  Not agreed; the chair will write to {ruler.the} {min.write}.
  Referred to a sub-committee, which {min.subc}.
  Agreed in principle; the money will be found {min.money}.
  The vote was tied; the chair's vote went with {min.tie}.
  Carried, with {#n} against, {min.after}.
  The discussion was {min.disc} and is {min.notmin}.
min.delay (people=4)
  a short adjournment for the members to calm down
  a recess for {drink}
  the second reading
  some argument about the wording
  a walk to look at the thing itself
  the treasurer had counted twice
  the chair had been fetched from the {drink} house
  a reading of the old charter
  a vote on whether to vote
  a long story about the founder
min.until (people=3)
  the next meeting
  {season.next}
  the figures come
  the {festival} holiday is over
  the weather improves
  someone remembers it
min.write (people=2)
  about it
  again
  in the plainest words
  this week
min.subc (people=3)
  has not met since {season.any}
  will report in {season.next}
  is the same people in other chairs
  meets at the {drink} house
  has lost its minutes
  has two members, who do not speak
  will meet when the weather allows
min.money (people=2)
  later
  somewhere
  from the {festival} fund
  by selling the old {min.building}
  by a collection at {holyplace}
  from the {craft} guild, who do not know it yet
  once the tolls are in
min.tie (people=3)
  the old arrangement
  the new one
  nobody, and the motion was withdrawn
  the side that had brought {drink}
  the members who had stayed awake
  whoever had spoken last
  the chair's own street
  the way of the founder
min.after (people=4)
  to some surprise
  after a long silence
  and the gallery cheered
  with two abstaining
  and the treasurer walked out
  to the relief of the chair
  after the member for the north side had been woken
  and the bell rang for the end of the shift
  without anyone saying why
  to nobody's satisfaction
  after the visitor had been asked to sit down
  with the {craft} guild against
min.notmin
  not minuted
  left out of these minutes
  best forgotten
  minuted elsewhere
min.disc (people=3)
  long
  heated
  personal
  circular
  short and bitter
  loud
  learned
  about something else
  tearful
  conducted in whispers

min.close (formula people=3)
  There being no other business, the meeting closed.
  The next meeting will be held when it is held.
  The meeting closed at ten. The tea urn was not working.
  The chair thanked the members, and the meeting closed.
  Meeting closed. The minutes are a fair record, as far as they go.
  The meeting closed in time for the last {msg.transit}.
)VG"
